-- title:
--   Commute GHalf Sandwich Move Chain Lift
-- statement:
--   **One move-chain lift preserves the adjacent operator relation.**
--
--   Let $(m,q,d)$ have a field model, let $\psi_{AB}$ be a bipartite quantum state, let $F$ be a slice-indexed polynomial family, and let $r\in\mathbb N$. Let $A$ and $B$ be operator families on $\mathsf{MoveQ}_r$ with outcomes in $\mathsf{MoveO}_r$. If
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{SDDOpRel}_{\psi_{AB},\,\operatorname{Unif}(\mathsf{MoveQ}_r)}(A,B;\delta),
--   $$
--
--   then the families $\mathsf L_r(F,A)$ and $\mathsf L_r(F,B)$ obtained by adjoining the next completed-slice factor on the left tensor register and reindexing the move-chain questions and outcomes satisfy
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{SDDOpRel}_{\psi_{AB},\,\operatorname{Unif}(\mathsf{MoveQ}_{r+1})}
--   \left(\mathsf L_r(F,A),\mathsf L_r(F,B);\delta\right).
--   $$
--
--   This is the recursive lift applied at each interior step of the move chain.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.commuteGHalfSandwich_moveChainLift`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/LionSR/MIPStarRE/blob/f382c801026f53a9efc260fdee707cb35e0adb15/MIPStarRE/LDT/Pasting/ComparisonLemmas/CommuteGHalfSandwich/MoveChain/Lifting.lean#L411-L553

